  "dialogue": {
    "text": "The fellow from the feed store borrowed twelve dollars—and this enamel mug—the same Tuesday. Returned neither. Three years later, he brought the mug back, plus a pie his wife made, apologizing like he'd misplaced the courthouse. I reached for my little ledger... then watched his hand shake. Keeping score tells you what you're owed. It can't tell you what a man is carrying. So I set the pencil down and poured him coffee. Funny thing: the account got lighter before the debt did. What are you carrying just because the ledger says so?",
    "language": "en-US",
    "rhubarb_extended_shapes": "GHX",
    "required_silence_return_shape": "X"
  },
